{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/documentation\/MISOComponents\/MISOPinCodeInput"},"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/7SwiftUI4ViewP"]}],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/documentation\/MISOComponents\/MISOPinCodeInput\/init(_:length:helperText:isOutlined:status:autofocus:)-10o29","doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/documentation\/MISOComponents\/MISOPinCodeInput\/init(_:length:helperText:isOutlined:status:autofocus:)-7psh2","doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/documentation\/MISOComponents\/MISOPinCodeInput\/init(_:length:helperText:tableName:bundle:isOutlined:status:autofocus:)"]},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/documentation\/MISOComponents\/MISOPinCodeInput\/body"]},{"anchor":"Type-Properties","title":"Type Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/documentation\/MISOComponents\/MISOPinCodeInput\/obfuscationCharacter","doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/documentation\/MISOComponents\/MISOPinCodeInput\/placeholderCharacter"]},{"anchor":"Enumerations","title":"Enumerations","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/documentation\/MISOComponents\/MISOPinCodeInput\/Length","doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/documentation\/MISOComponents\/MISOPinCodeInput\/Status"]},{"anchor":"Default-Implementations","title":"Default Implementations","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/documentation\/MISOComponents\/MISOPinCodeInput\/View-Implementations","doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/documentation\/MISOComponents\/MISOPinCodeInput\/View-Implementations"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/documentation\/MISOComponents"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MISOPinCodeInput","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MISOPinCodeInput","modules":[{"name":"Components"}],"externalID":"s:14MISOComponents16MISOPinCodeInputV","symbolKind":"struct","platforms":[{"introducedAt":"15.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false,"name":"iOS","deprecated":false},{"introducedAt":"1.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false,"name":"visionOS","deprecated":false}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MISOPinCodeInput","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"PIN code input is a UI element that allows to capture short, fixed-length numeric codes, typically for authentication or confirmation purposes,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"such as a four, six or eight-digit personal identification number (PIN)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"PIN code input is presented as a series of individual input fields or boxes, each representing a single digit, to enhance readability and encourage accurate input,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"while supporting smooth keyboard navigation and secured input masking if needed."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@"},{"kind":"attribute","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM","text":"MainActor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"MISOPinCodeInput","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Layouts","type":"heading","anchor":"Layouts","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The component can be rendered as two different layouts:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"outlined"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" layout: A minimalist input with a transparent background and a visible stroke outlining the field.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"This style may be interesting for contexts other than form pages, e.g. when inputs need to feel lightweight and unobtrusive,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in a header (search field), or in a selection\/filtering feature in a product catalog","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not outlined"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (default): An input with a subtle background fill and visible bottom border, creating a softer and more contained look."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Best suited for dense layouts or to enhance visibility."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The component provides 3 layouts for the input: 4 boxes, 6 boxes or 8 boxes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A helper text can be used to support text to convey additional information about the input field, such as how it will be used."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It should ideally only take up a single line, though may wrap to multiple lines if required, and be either persistently visible or visible only on focus."}]},{"text":"Error status","anchor":"Error-status","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The Error status indicates that the user input does not meet validation rules or expected formatting.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"It provides immediate visual feedback, typically through a red border, error icon, and a clear, accessible error message positioned below the input (mandatory).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"This state helps users quickly identify and correct mistakes by explaining what went wrong and, when possible, how to fix it.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The input remains editable, encouraging users to revise their input without starting over.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The error state must be triggered by an explicit validation (submission, API response), and not in real time with each keystroke.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"This can occur either because the entered code does not match the expected code, because the user entered an expired or already used code,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or finally if the maximum number of attempts has been exceeded."}]},{"text":"Specific design guidelines","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Specific-design-guidelines"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In the context of a PIN code input, in addition to the input’s “Error” UI rendering, it is essential to also include an “Alert” component"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"(also in its “Error” status) in the interface.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Particular cases","anchor":"Particular-cases","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/documentation\/MISOComponents\/MISOPinCodeInput","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" component supports autofill feature of values like OTP code."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"For example if the user receives a message with inside a code the system can extract, the keyboard can suggest to the user to fill it.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"If the digits fits the component, it will be filled."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"If the digits are longer, they will be truncated.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"If the digits are shorter, they will be filled, letting other fields empty."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The copy\/paste feature is also available and has the same behavior.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Technical considerations","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Technical-considerations"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For some cases, on phones screens or with 8 boxes in iPhone, you may need to use a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScrollView"},{"type":"text","text":" to embed the component and let user move it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["ScrollView(.horizontal) {","    MISOPinCodeInput($value,","                     length: .eight,","                     helperText: \"Enter your secret code sent to your phone\")","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Note also the exposed ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"value","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Binding"},{"text":" will be updated when all digits are written.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Accessibility considerations","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Accessibility-considerations"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The content of the fields is vocalized by Voice Over; the placeholders (defined in "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/documentation\/MISOComponents\/MISOPinCodeInput\/obfuscationCharacter"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/documentation\/MISOComponents\/MISOPinCodeInput\/placeholderCharacter","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":")"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are not vocalized to let users know what they wrote."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The component gets only numeric values, not letters or symbols, only numbers."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Depending on the component configuration, autofocus can still be used when the component appears, and focus is moved to the next field as digits are entered."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For example if Voice Over is enavled, the autoficus is disabled."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The component and its digit fields are vocalized with internal wording."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When using the error status, provide a clear, concise error message explaining what went wrong and, when possible, how to fix it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(for example: "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"“The code you entered is invalid. Try again.”","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use helper text to communicate additional guidance (for example: "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“Check the 6‑digit code sent by SMS”"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":"), and keep this text short so it remains easy to vocalize"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and understand."}]},{"anchor":"Rich-text","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Rich text"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Rich text can be used for error and helper texts.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Strong text can be used sparingly to highlight key information within the content."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"No other text styles should be used."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Underlined text must not be applied manually (e.g. in error message), as it is commonly associated with hyperlinks and may mislead users."}]},{"anchor":"Code-samples","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Code samples"},{"code":["    \/\/ The value with the code","    @State private var pinCode: String = \"\"","","    \/\/ By default, the PIN code input displays only 6 boxes","    MISOPinCodeInput($pinCode)","","    \/\/ It can have also up 4 or 8 boxes, with an helper text","    MISOPinCodeInput($pinCode, length: .eight, helperText: \"Enter your 8 secret digits\")","","    \/\/ The component can be used in error contexts","    MISOPinCodeInput($pinCode, length: .six, status: .error(message: \"The OTP code you entered is not correct\"))"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"name":"Version","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1.3.0 (Figma component design version)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"},{"name":"Since","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDS 1.4.0"}]}],"style":"note"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/misocomponents\/misopincodeinput"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://MISOComponents/documentation/MISOComponents/MISOPinCodeInput/Length":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Length"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/misocomponents\/misopincodeinput\/length","title":"MISOPinCodeInput.Length","abstract":[{"text":"The type of layout to apply to the ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"pin code input"}]},{"text":" to define the size of the input","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/documentation\/MISOComponents\/MISOPinCodeInput\/Length","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Length"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://MISOComponents/documentation/MISOComponents":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/documentation\/MISOComponents","url":"\/documentation\/misocomponents","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The catalog of all components provided by MISO. It contains also "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View"},{"text":" extensions and ","type":"text"},{"code":"ViewModifiers","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to apply tokens and styles on components and higher-level views.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","images":[{"type":"icon","identifier":"ic_folder_categories.png"}],"type":"topic","title":"Components"},"doc://MISOComponents/documentation/MISOComponents/MISOPinCodeInput/View-Implementations":{"url":"\/documentation\/misocomponents\/misopincodeinput\/view-implementations","type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","title":"View Implementations","identifier":"doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/documentation\/MISOComponents\/MISOPinCodeInput\/View-Implementations","abstract":[],"kind":"article"},"doc://MISOComponents/documentation/MISOComponents/MISOPinCodeInput/placeholderCharacter":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/misocomponents\/misopincodeinput\/placeholdercharacter","title":"placeholderCharacter","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/documentation\/MISOComponents\/MISOPinCodeInput\/placeholderCharacter","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"placeholderCharacter"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The symbol used as a placeholder for a digit not yet filled.","type":"text"}]},"doc://MISOComponents/documentation/MISOComponents/MISOPinCodeInput/Status":{"title":"MISOPinCodeInput.Status","url":"\/documentation\/misocomponents\/misopincodeinput\/status","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Define all available status for the PIN code input","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/documentation\/MISOComponents\/MISOPinCodeInput\/Status","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Status","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Status","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://MISOComponents/documentation/MISOComponents/MISOPinCodeInput/obfuscationCharacter":{"url":"\/documentation\/misocomponents\/misopincodeinput\/obfuscationcharacter","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"static","